  "findings": [
    "Both historical serving first token differences reproduce as actual selected-token differences at the same prefix in the frozen production implementation.",
    "OFF produces tied maximum logits at those positions. Its highest-index argmax rule chooses the larger token ID; ON maxima remain unique and match the independent reference.",
    "Luminal decomposed/frontend and CUDA fused argmax intentionally agree on highest-index tie breaking. This is not a CUDA-only argmax bug.",
    "Applying a canonical lowest-ID argmax to all exported rows yields reference agreement for both arms. This observation does not change deployed sampling semantics or establish a numerical tolerance.",
    "Whole-graph schedules differ in several providers, including the decode LM head. These data do not isolate which operator creates the numerical shift, prove a shared-quantization regression, or qualify performance."
  ],
